NanoPC-T6 LTS device tree overlays
==================================

This package builds rk3588-nanopc-t6-lts.dtb from the linux6.18 kernel source
with __symbols__ (dtc -@), plus a set of overlays, and fails the build if any
overlay does not apply to that DTB. Everything is installed into the kernel's
versioned dtbs directory:

  /boot/dtbs/dtbs-<kernver>/rockchip/rk3588-nanopc-t6-lts-symbols.dtb
  /boot/dtbs/dtbs-<kernver>/rockchip/overlays/nanopc-t6-*.dtbo

The rk3588-nanopc-t6-lts.dtb shipped by linux6.18 has no __symbols__, so
U-Boot cannot apply overlays to it. Boot the -symbols DTB instead.

Requirements
------------
- U-Boot booting via extlinux, with CONFIG_OF_LIBFDT_OVERLAY (implied by
  ROCKCHIP_RK3588 in mainline U-Boot).
- u-boot-menu with FDTOVERLAYS support.
- The exact linux6.18 version this package was built for. When linux6.18 is
  updated, bump version, _kernrev and checksum in the template and rebuild;
  xbps refuses the kernel update until this package matches.

Enabling
--------
No overlays are enabled by default. In /etc/default/extlinux:

  DTBPATH="rockchip/rk3588-nanopc-t6-lts-symbols.dtb"
  FDTOVERLAYS="rockchip/overlays/nanopc-t6-eth-aliases.dtbo rockchip/overlays/nanopc-t6-uart4.dtbo"

Both are relative to the kernel's dtbs-<kernver> directory. Then regenerate
/boot/extlinux/extlinux.conf:

  # xbps-reconfigure -f linux6.18

Overlays
--------
nanopc-t6-eth-aliases.dtbo
  Describes the two onboard RTL8125 2.5G controllers and aliases them to
  ethernet0/ethernet1, so U-Boot writes the eFuse-derived MAC addresses into
  the DT before Linux probes (stable MACs, no udev rule needed).

nanopc-t6-uartN.dtbo (N = 0, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8)
  Enables uartN on the 40-pin header. Each overlay works on its own. The
  header routes uart0, uart4 and uart7 to a different pin group than the SoC
  default (m1), so those overlays also override pinctrl-0.

  UART   Header TX/RX   GPIO          Pin group
  uart0   8 / 10        GPIO0_C5/C4   uart0m0_xfer  (overrides SoC default)
  uart3  29 / 31        GPIO3_B6/B5   uart3m1_xfer
  uart4  23 / 19        GPIO1_B3/B2   uart4m2_xfer  (overrides SoC default)
  uart6  28 / 27        GPIO1_A1/A0   uart6m1_xfer
  uart7  22 / 24        GPIO1_B5/B4   uart7m2_xfer  (overrides SoC default)
  uart8  40 / 36        GPIO3_A2/A3   uart8m1_xfer

  uart2 is the debug console on its own header and is already enabled.

Pin contention
--------------
Header pins are shared between functions, and whichever overlay claims a pin
last wins. uart4 and uart7 overlap SPI0; uart3 overlaps I2S2 and PWM. Do not
enable conflicting functions together.
